<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Oglethorpe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1696–1785</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as James Edward Oglethorpe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James Oglethorpe was an English soldier, member of Parliament and philanthropist who founded the colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>. In 1732 he led the board of Trustees that obtained a charter for the land between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savannah">Savannah</a> and Altamaha rivers, intended as a refuge for the poor and a buffer against Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>. He founded Savannah in 1733 with the help of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamacraw">Yamacraw</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomochichi">Tomochichi</a> and defeated the Spanish at Bloody Marsh in 1742.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-oglethorpe.jpg" alt="James Oglethorpe" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alfred Edmund Dyer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:James_Edward_Oglethorpe.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
